### Who was the 39th President of the United States, and from which institution did that president earn an undergraduate degree?
Answer: The 39th President of the United States was Jimmy Carter, who earned his undergraduate degree from the United States Naval Academy—a public service academy. As the search result notes, "only nine presidents have received their undergraduate degrees from public universities (including the service academies)," with Carter being one of them.

