## Final Judgement
**1. Summary of key insights:**  
The fact-check reveals that while Joe Biden earned his bachelor's degree from the University of Delaware (a non-Ivy League institution), several U.S. presidents before him were elected without Ivy League undergraduate degrees. For example, Bill Clinton attended Georgetown University, Ronald Reagan attended Eureka College, and Jimmy Carter attended the United States Naval Academy—none of which are Ivy League members. Therefore, the claim that Biden would be the first president without an Ivy League degree if elected is contradicted by these historical precedents.

**2. Information still lacking:**  
No critical information is missing; the evidence clearly identifies multiple prior presidents without Ivy League undergraduate degrees.

**3. Conclusion:**  
Based on the recorded evidence, the claim is explicitly refuted because multiple former U.S. presidents were elected without holding Ivy League undergraduate degrees, so Biden would not be the first. Therefore, the final decision is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is refuted because multiple previous U.S. presidents were elected without Ivy League undergraduate degrees, including [Bill Clinton (Georgetown University)](https://www.trade-schools.net/learn/presidential-colleges), [Ronald Reagan (Eureka College)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_heads_of_state_educated_in_the_United_States), and [Jimmy Carter (United States Naval Academy)](https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2014/05/22/degree-from-harvard-or-yale-most-americans-say-it-doesnt-matter-for-their-president/). Although [Joe Biden's degree is from the non-Ivy League University of Delaware](https://www.businessinsider.com/quiz-politicians-yearbook-2010-9), he would not be the first president without an Ivy League degree.